; fixx.inix -- Dean's transform job, corrected.
;
; Two notes on what changed:
;
; 1. The key names are Find, Replace, Options, Extract, Divider.  Lower case
;    (find=, replace=) now works too, but these are the canonical spellings.
;
; 2. A leading space in a Replace value is easy to lose, because the value can be
;    trimmed when the job is read.  Replace values are unescaped, so write a
;    leading space as \x20 and it always survives.  That is the only change to
;    the expressions themselves.
;
; Remember: the document you have OPEN when you run Transform Files (Alt+=)
; must contain the LIST of files to transform, one full path per line -- for
; example a single line reading
;   C:\Users\Dean\Documents\watermelon snow.txt
; The open document is not itself the file that gets transformed.
;
; Run it on a COPY first, and use Test mode to see the match counts before Run.

[print page numbers]
Find=\n\-{5,}
Replace=\x20x

[braille page indicators]
Find=(\s{2,})([0-9a-eptx]+)\n
Replace=

[linebreak]
Find=\n([^\n\s])
Replace=\x20$1
